    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pick\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThis bug is a reproduction of the issue which I mentioned in discussion. Below is the source code to reproduce it. I made it as simple as possible.\r\n[try.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/16829230/try.zip)\r\n\r\nTo give some context, I deal with json files as large as 5MB+ at work and most of the lines are very big in those jsons. I was able to see noticable delay with it when navigating through those json files.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nnightly latest\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Unzip the zip file attached in description and navigate to the unzipped directory where trial.lua and 9.OeaLULSY.js exist.\r\n2. Run the command ``nvim -u trial.lua 9.OeaLULSY.js``.\r\n3. Once lazy.nvim downloads the plugins necessary and finishes everything run buf_lines picker using ``Pick buf_lines``\r\n4. Press `<tab>` to open preview and press the `<up>` key continuously for a second and leave it after some time. You can see that there is a lag between input keys and the movement of the UI and the UI still moves even after you stop pressing the `<up>` key.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nNo lag\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nLag",
