            "body": "To be frank, this is a very rare scenario and I dont think most people will deal with such files. It sucks to be me since I have to deal with such files. Anyways all I can say is fzf with fzf-lua works like a charm without any input lag in such scenario since it runs in a seperate thread and is written in go which is compiled and is much faster than lua. So you can actually ignore this bug if you think it is not relevant afaik.",
